Usage: copilot plugin enable <name>

Enable an installed plugin by name.

Accepts a bare `name`, a marketplace-qualified `name@marketplace`,
or a direct-install source id. The change is persisted to your
configuration and applies to future sessions.

Arguments:
  <name>
          Plugin name, name@marketplace, or direct-install source id

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  # Enable a marketplace plugin
  $ copilot plugin enable arch@awesome-copilot

  # Enable a plugin by bare name
  $ copilot plugin enable my-plugin

Learn More:
  Use `copilot <command> --help` for more information about a command.
  Read the documentation at https://docs.github.com/copilot/how-tos/copilot-cli
